  "findings": {
    "duplicated_initialization": [
      {
        "observation": "B runs stock calibration configuration and initialization, reads stock EtaJES, GSC and JMS assets, prepares MC and pseudo-data uncertainty tool assets in both radii, and initializes the stock small-R NN graph, cuts, scale-factor file and large-R FF tables. The overlay lazily initializes the provider and parses its CorrectionSet at the first binding. The same calibration data thus enter stock setup and the replacement payload. Retained stock setup also provides tool configuration and systematic metadata.",
        "evidence": [
          "selected_job_log",
          "selected_job_runtime_inputs",
          "framework_runtime",
          "nominal_jet_setup",
          "small_nominal_pileup",
          "nominal_eta_jes",
          "small_nominal_gsc",
          "large_nominal_jms",
          "uncertainty_adapter",
          "small_jvt_update",
          "small_jvt_selection",
          "stock_jvt_efficiency_file_load",
          "native_nnjvt_graph",
          "b_large_ff"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "retained_framework_work": [
      {
        "observation": "Stock algorithms still determine the applicable state list, route MC and pseudo-data states, request per-state shallow copies, read preselection, decorate truth/validity, and write ROOT output. The stock uncertainty tool filters variations and sets up and caches UncertaintySet before the replaced scalar calculation. The FF algorithm requests its output copy before the FF-name guard. This includes a nominal copy with zero FF smearing calls and ordinary-state pass-through copies in full mode.",
        "evidence": [
          "stock_uncertainty_algorithm",
          "uncertainty_adapter",
          "stock_ff_algorithm",
          "selected_job_log"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "replacement_and_repeat_work": [
      {
        "observation": "Nominal small-R pileup, EtaJES, GSC and NNJvt update, selection and scale-factor calculations delegate to native nodes. Nominal large-R EtaJES, JMS and acceptance delegate as well. Both radii still dispatch ordinary uncertainty with NOSYS. The selected full trace shows the nominal calibration stages ran once per corresponding source jet.",
        "evidence": [
          "small_nominal_pileup",
          "nominal_eta_jes",
          "small_nominal_gsc",
          "small_jvt_update",
          "small_jvt_selection",
          "small_jvt_efficiency",
          "large_nominal_jms",
          "uncertainty_adapter",
          "selected_job_trace"
        ]
      },
      {
        "observation": "Ordinary uncertainty uses an 18-value scalar input vector and rebuilds the state name per jet. It retrieves existing EventInfo and reads the jet data and availability flags. Small-R NNJvt updates repack event vertex columns across update passes. The observed event-input count is aggregate across call sites and cannot identify how many calls came from each site.",
        "evidence": [
          "framework_runtime",
          "framework_event_columns",
          "nominal_jet_setup",
          "small_jvt_update",
          "uncertainty_adapter",
          "selected_job_trace"
        ]
      },
      {
        "observation": "The pT/rapidity bridge and the mass bridge each call the same large_selection node and each consumes one mask. On jets reaching both bridges, rapidity and both sets of cuts are evaluated twice. The trace gives the combined number of calls, so it does not establish the number of duplicated pairs.",
        "evidence": [
          "b_large_pt_accept",
          "b_large_mass_accept",
          "native_large_selection",
          "selected_job_trace"
        ]
      },
      {
        "observation": "The selected portable provider consumes native values with no xAOD or ROOT link dependency. Its ordinary uncertainty path avoids the earlier release-backed adapter's private xAOD Jet and EventInfo. Its FF call bypasses the stock matched private xAOD Jet. The surrounding B bridge continues to read stock xAOD objects, translate statuses and write the stock output four-vector and decorations.",
        "evidence": [
          "selected_native_dependencies",
          "portable_uncertainty_input",
          "native_uncertainty",
          "earlier_release_backed_private_objects",
          "stock_ff_private_jet",
          "b_large_ff",
          "uncertainty_adapter"
        ]
      },
      {
        "observation": "The B FF adapter re-reads R10 truth, materializes four ordered coordinates and leases the generic truth context per call. Its borrowed context takes the uncached native matching path. C binds an owned R10 context for its physical chunks. Direct C starts the full-mode signed-pair reuse protocol for small and combined scopes; the B scalar adapter does not enter that protocol.",
        "evidence": [
          "b_large_ff",
          "framework_borrowed_truth",
          "native_large_matching",
          "native_uncertainty",
          "shipped_visible_script"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "timing_boundary": {
      "observation": "The observed B qualification wall is an instrumented full observer job. Earlier round-zero timings used a different provider. Use retained matched production B/A receipts to judge the 1.20 budget. These mechanisms do not assign a share of elapsed time to a specific operation.",
