  "conditional_b_only_trial": {
    "status": "Design only",
    "trigger": "If the retained large-R or combined B/A budget misses or straddles 1.20, measure one mechanism at a time before considering a production change.",
    "first_candidate": "Retain both stock acceptance handles, sequencing, preselection and decorations. Evaluate the existing native three-output acceptance once and supply the matching per-jet, per-systematic cached mass mask to the existing mass bridge when the prerequisite pT/rapidity bridge ran on the same unchanged inputs. Use an explicitly event-scoped or per-copy ephemeral cache. Bind to exact pT/eta/phi/m bits and tool configuration, and preserve the current independent mass calculation if the cache is absent, stale or inapplicable. Do not change output keys or introduce a persistent aux branch. Preserve the exact cut encoding, including nonfinite and boundary behavior.",
    "independently_testable_candidate": "For FF, lazily prepare a read-only R10 truth snapshot or lease once per event and configured collection key. Preserve EventContext isolation, availability and retrieval/error behavior, truth order, equal-distance tie breaking, p4 bits and labels. Ensure the view lives for precisely the event or systematic processing scope, and releases safely on early return and exceptions. Keep the numerical stock-equivalent matching implementation and its thresholds constant in the first trial so packing reuse is the only change.",
    "checks": [
      "Use the same original PHYSLITE UUID, release, scope, provider and payload as the baseline, with a new opt-in adapter variant and an independently recorded hash.",
      "On a 128-event nominal and full large-R/combined smoke, require exact observer and histogram comparisons against stock and current B, including p4, validity and selection masks, weight/status decorations, missing or empty truth behavior, stable event/object order, branch names and state names. Exercise stale or missing acceptance reuse and truth lease cleanup in a bounded fixture.",
      "If the smoke passes, time up to four rotated stock/current-B/candidate-B full-file pairs in an admitted single-thread, quiet window, retaining the same output and input contracts. Compare candidate/current B wall and candidate/stock A against 1.20 with the normal per-pair spread and resource checks. Trace only a separate diagnostic pair to confirm the intended call or packing reduction."
    ]
  },
